<!--Gem_Page_Main_Editor--><div class="clearfix"></div><div class="gryffeditor"><div data-label="Parallax" data-key="parallax" data-atomgroup="module" id="m-1777537303777" class="module-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-parallax" data-ver="2" data-id="1777537303777"><div class="gf_parallax-container"><div class="gf_parallax-bg"></div></div><div class="module gf_parallax " data-image="https://ucarecdn.com/cc536c88-afc1-4bda-9be0-b8bae94a751c/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/PC_Xone_KV_v2.0_20260307.webp" data-speed-xs="1" data-speed-sm="1" data-speed-md="0.5" data-option="" data-speed-lg="0.5"><span data-index="1" class="item-content"><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1777537274916" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1777537274916"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center" data-gemlang="en"><h1 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2"><span style="color: rgb(230, 232, 233);">The Evolution of X one : Why we rebuilt the UV, Laser & UV-DTF all-in-one experience</span></h1></div></div></span></div></div><!--gfsplit--><div data-label="Separator" data-key="separator" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776845803256" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-separator" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1776845803256"><div class="elm gf-elm-center gf-elm-center-lg gf-elm-center-xs gf-elm-center-sm gf-elm-center-md" data-align="left" data-exc=""><hr class="gf_separator"></div></div><!--gfsplit--><div data-label="Row" data-key="row" data-atomgroup="row" id="r-1776845246948" class="gf_row" data-icon="gpicon-row" data-id="1776845246948" data-layout-lg="12" data-extraclass="" data-layout-md="12" data-layout-sm="12" data-layout-xs="12" style="display: block;"><div class="gf_column gf_col-lg-12 gf_col-md-12 gf_col-sm-12 gf_col-xs-12" id="c-1776845246957" data-id="1776845246957"><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" id="e-1776845174417" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1776845174417" data-resolution="3000x3000" style="display: block;"><div class="elm gf-elm-center gf_elm-left-xs gf-elm-left-lg gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs" data-exc=""><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/8f09f402-a489-4448-b813-e8f188136ca9/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/" alt="" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="auto" data-height="auto" title="" natural-width="46" natural-height="46" width="46" height="46"></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" id="e-1776833704613" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776833704613"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p>For years, bringing a multi-layered design to life meant juggling three machines — a UV printer, a laser engraver, and a separate UV-DTF setup. We realized it was time to build a system that works the way creators actually think.</p></div></div><div data-label="Separator" data-key="separator" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776845769009" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-separator" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1776845769009"><div class="elm gf-elm-center" data-align="left"><hr class="gf_separator"></div></div></div></div><!--gfsplit--><div data-label="Row" data-key="row" id="r-1776833704547" class="gf_row" data-icon="gpicon-row" data-id="1776833704547" data-extraclass="" data-layout-sm="12+12"><div class="gf_column gf_col-lg-8 gf_col-md-8 gf_col-xs-12 gf_col-sm-12" id="c-1615193175561" data-id="1615193175561"><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776839192314" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776839192314"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h2 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">Phase 1: Idea of X one</h2></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776850809779" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776850809779"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf_gs-text-paragraph-1" data-gemlang="en"><p>The idea for the X one was born from the true voices of thousands of real customers. <strong>Key, <a href="https://www.procolored.com/pages/our-brand-procolored" class="" target="_blank">our co-founder</a> and a UV expert with over 10 years of specialization,</strong> brought his deep insight directly to the source—immersing himself in forums, Reddit threads, Facebook groups, and YouTube comment sections to understand the raw experiences of creators juggling separate UV printers and laser engravers.</p><p>As a Co-founder who has led Procolored to become a pioneer in the desktop UV printer market since 2018, earning the trust of over 150,000 users worldwide, Key should have felt a sense of accomplishment. But for a relentless innovator who is always chasing the 'next big thing', standing still was never an option.&nbsp;</p><p>He remained deeply embedded in the creator community, and it was through these ongoing conversations that he uncovered a truth the rest of the industry was ignoring: <strong>Laser creators were constantly striving to find ways to graft full-color onto their engravings to fully realize the potential of their crafts and ideas.</strong></p><p><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/580f0214-75ab-4870-b37c-4cfb507f3b60/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/Laser%20Engraving%20Color-Fill%20Tutorials%20%E2%80%94%20Popular%20YouTube%20Videos.jpg" alt="Top YouTube tutorials on laser engraving color fill techniques, featuring Laser Engraving 911 and Laser Everything" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="2892" height="3000" natural-width="2892" natural-height="3000"></p><p>But the only solutions available were to do it manually or to buy a second UV machine. That’s when an "integrated idea" came to Key’s mind: <strong>Why not create an all-in-one machine that combines UV full-color printing and laser engraving into one?&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p></div></div><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776850785190" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776850785190"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h2 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">Phase 2: The Research—Digging into the "Invisible" Trenches</h2></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776852671312" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776852671312"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf_gs-text-paragraph-1" data-gemlang="en"><p>When the "all-in-one" concept was born, a wave of excitement swept through the team. Key immediately mobilized  R&D and marketing departments to conduct deeper, more comprehensive research.</p><p>While the marketing team conducted extensive one-on-one surveys to build a reliable data foundation, the R&D team dove back into the trenches of forums and creator groups to uncover the hidden technical friction.</p><p><strong>The signals from the market were overwhelming: 98% of creators expressed an eager desire for an integrated machine. </strong>However, beneath this excitement, our research revealed deep-seated anxieties and technical bottlenecks:</p></div></div><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776852629095" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776852629095"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h3 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">The Smelly, Tedious Pre-coating Process:</h3></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" id="e-1776833704635" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776833704635"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf_gs-text-paragraph-1 gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><p><span style="font-size: inherit; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em; letter-spacing: 0px; background-color: transparent;">We’ve listened to countless creators who are simply exhausted by the "chemical trial-and-error" of traditional UV primers. As ProColorGraphics once shared: <strong>"Ink and cleaner smells don't normally bother me, but the adhesion promoter he used was bad."</strong> While some "low-odor" promoters have emerged recently, they merely mask the issue rather than solving it.</span><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/54d496a7-9870-4ca5-9f3f-9307c8cb3228/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/customer-review-ap3115-primer-smell-2018%20_1_.png" alt="" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1200" height="214" natural-width="1200" natural-height="214" style="font-size: inherit; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em; letter-spacing: 0px; background-color: transparent;"><br><span style="background-color: transparent; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em;">For beginners, mastering adhesion across different materials wasn’t just an extra step—it was a daunting learning curve.&nbsp;</span><br><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/49a1c05b-ccef-4553-955f-f2f78f5f0c13/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/customer-precoating-question-2020-05-08.png" alt="" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1341" height="640" natural-width="1341" natural-height="640" style="font-size: inherit; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em; letter-spacing: 0px; background-color: transparent;"><br><span style="background-color: transparent; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em;">We saw the same recurring plea in every expert’s comment section: "Which primer do you actually recommend?"&nbsp;</span><br><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/8778ce77-d65a-4a8e-90de-11972f6b73d5/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/customer-youtube-comment-uv-leather-adhesion%20_1_.png" alt="" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1200" height="319" natural-width="1200" natural-height="319" style="font-size: inherit; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em; letter-spacing: 0px; background-color: transparent;"><br><span style="background-color: transparent; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px; text-align: inherit; word-spacing: 0.001em;">For many, this technical barrier was the wall where great ideas went to die, leaving brilliant concepts stuck on the drawing board.  <strong>Between the smell, the mess, and the guesswork of choosing the right promoter, pre-coating had become the single biggest frustration standing in the way of every UV printer user.</strong></span><br></p></div></div><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776853105194" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776853105194"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-lg gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h3 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">The Manual Alignment Frustration:</h3></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776853257945" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776853257945"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf_gs-text-paragraph-1" data-gemlang="en"><p>We felt the "pain in the rear" of creators struggling with manual alignment. As one user put it, using crosshairs often led to being "always off by half a millimeter," turning expensive materials into wasted scrap in a matter of seconds.</p><p><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/8f177db6-8c60-4588-870b-757a7fa0baf3/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/customer-review-uv11-pro-alignment-waste.png" alt="" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1200" height="372" natural-width="1200" natural-height="372"></p><p><br></p></div></div><div data-label="Row" data-key="row" data-atomgroup="row" id="r-1776914590911" class="gf_row" data-icon="gpicon-row" data-id="1776914590911" data-layout-lg="6+6" data-extraclass="" data-layout-md="6+6" data-layout-sm="6+6" data-layout-xs="12+12"><div class="gf_column gf_col-lg-6 gf_col-md-6 gf_col-sm-6 gf_col-xs-12" id="c-1776914590868" data-id="1776914590868"><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776853360554" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1776853360554" data-resolution="3000x3000"><div class="elm gf-elm-center gf_elm-left-xs gf-elm-center-lg gf-elm-center-md gf-elm-center-sm gf-elm-center-xs" data-exc=""><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/c946c3a8-286e-41a6-8818-40e938ab3018/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/customer-alignment-grid-issue-2021-03-21.png" alt="" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1341" height="609" natural-width="1341" natural-height="609"></div></div></div><div class="gf_column gf_col-lg-6 gf_col-md-6 gf_col-sm-6 gf_col-xs-12" id="c-1776914592135" data-id="1776914592135"><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776853603560" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1776853603560" data-resolution="3000x3000"><div class="elm gf-elm-center gf_elm-left-xs gf-elm-center-lg gf-elm-center-md gf-elm-center-sm gf-elm-center-xs" data-exc=""><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/f2d6ffbb-7db0-4ca6-a438-b562f9ae4083/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/customer-alignment-settings-issue-2021-03-21.png" alt="UV printer user frustrated with manual alignment and conflicting tutorial settings" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="1341" height="759" natural-width="1341" natural-height="759"></div></div></div></div><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776853653617" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776853653617"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h3 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">The Printhead Clog Anxiety:&nbsp;</h3></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776853683935" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776853683935"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf_gs-text-paragraph-1" data-gemlang="en"><p>A major concern loomed over the "all-in-one" dream: the high risk of laser dust clogging and destroying delicate UV <a href="https://www.procolored.com/blogs/news/do-you-know-why-ink-clogs-the-printheads" class="">print heads</a>—a collision of two technologies that seemed, on the surface, incompatible.</p><p>Beyond these, users voiced clear demands for the future: the machine had to be compact, aesthetically high-end, affordable for small businesses, and intelligent enough to eliminate a steep learning curve. <strong>It became clear: to build the X one, we weren’t just merging two tools; we were rescuing creators from a broken, exhausting workflow.</strong></p><p></p></div></div></div><div class="gf_column gf_col-lg-4 gf_col-md-4 gf_col-xs-12 gf_col-sm-12" id="c-1615193183766" data-id="1615193183766"></div></div><!--gfsplit--><div data-label="Row" data-key="row" id="r-1776833704599" class="gf_row" data-icon="gpicon-row" data-id="1776833704599" data-extraclass=""><div class="gf_column gf_col-lg-8 gf_col-md-8 gf_col-sm-8 gf_col-xs-12" id="c-1615193175561" data-id="1615193175561"><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776840043395" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776840043395"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs gf-elm-left-lg" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h2 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">Phase 3: The Breakthrough — Overcoming the "Impossible"&nbsp;</h2><h2 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">(2024-2025)</h2></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776915215298" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776915215298"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf_gs-text-paragraph-1" data-gemlang="en"><p><span style="color: rgb(20, 20, 20); font-size: 16px; word-spacing: 0.016px;">Empowered by strong market demand and Key’s passion for innovation, our team embarked on a challenging but determined journey. We addressed every user pain point one by one, turning "bugs" into core "features":</span></p></div></div><div data-label="Image" data-key="image" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776915140492" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-image" data-ver="1.0" data-id="1776915140492" data-resolution="3000x3000"><div class="elm gf-elm-center gf_elm-left-xs gf-elm-center-lg gf-elm-center-md gf-elm-center-sm gf-elm-center-xs" data-exc=""><img src="https://ucarecdn.com/dc959192-14e7-46b3-9055-50864a9c0fc9/-/format/auto/-/preview/3000x3000/-/quality/lighter/x-one-uv-printer-home-studio-breakthrough.webp" alt="Procolored X One UV printer and laser engraver in a home studio, surrounded by printed phone cases, wood engravings, and sticker artwork" class="gf_image" data-gemlang="en" data-width="100%" data-height="auto" title="" width="2000" height="1042" natural-width="2000" natural-height="1042"></div></div><div data-label="Heading" data-key="heading" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776914752559" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-heading" data-ver="2" data-id="1776914752559"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-center gf-elm-left-lg gf-elm-left-md gf-elm-left-sm gf-elm-left-xs" data-gemlang="en" data-exc=""><h3 class="gf_gs-text-heading-2">Zero-Error Camera Auto Precision:</h3></div></div><div data-label="Text Block" data-key="text-block" data-atomgroup="element" id="e-1776914794753" class="element-wrap" data-icon="gpicon-textblock" data-ver="1" data-id="1776914794753"><div class="elm text-edit gf-elm-left gf_gs-text-paragraph-1" data-gemlang="en"><p><span style="--tw-border-spacing-y: 0; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; color: inherit; font-family: inherit;